Cueson command-line interface.

Usage:
  cueson [global options] <command>

Commands:
  encode      Encode a subtitle source as Cue JSON.
  restore     Restore exact source-envelope bytes.
  render      Render Cue JSON from its structured model.
  convert     Convert SubRip and WebVTT through the common model.
  validate    Validate Cue JSON or a native subtitle without output.
  inspect     Inspect safe structural facts about an input.
  schema      Print or save the embedded Cue JSON schema.
  version     Print the Cueson executable version.
  completion  Generate static shell completion.

Global options:
  -q, --quiet  Suppress informational and success diagnostics.
  --silent     Suppress every non-error diagnostic.
  --no-color   Disable diagnostic color.
  -h, --help   Show help.
  --           End option processing; following paths and operands remain literal.

Streams:
  stdout  Payload data and explicit help only; never diagnostics or decoration.
  stderr  Diagnostics, warnings, errors, and error-associated short usage.
  Quiet and silent never suppress an explicitly requested stdout payload.

Exit codes:
  0  Command or explicit help completed successfully; warnings may be present.
  1  An accepted operation failed during processing, cancellation, or runtime I/O.
  2  Command syntax, an operand, an option, or a pre-execution requirement was invalid.

Examples:
  cueson --help
  cueson validate captions.srt
  cueson inspect --json document.cueson.json
  cueson convert captions.vtt --to srt
  cueson completion bash
